I'm not sure if this is what you're looking for, but you can do this:

Create a new folder in your project called "HelloWorld"
Create a new file called "HelloWorld.cs" with the following code:
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

namespace HelloWorld
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Hello World!");
            Console.ReadLine();
        }
    }
}

Compile and run the program.

